<h1>Spiral Conveyor Systems</h1>
<p class="usa-intro">A spiral conveyor is a vertical conveyor that moves products between elevation levels along a helical path wrapped around a central column. Products enter and exit at the same time, so flow stays continuous with no batch cycling. Spirals serve <a href="/industries/packaging-line-conveyors/">packaging lines</a>, distribution centers, and food plants where floor space is limited and throughput rules out batch lifts like <a href="/conveyor-types/vertical-reciprocating/">vertical reciprocating conveyors (VRCs)</a>.</p>
<p>The main buying decisions are the vertical conveyor type (spiral, VRC, or incline), modular or custom construction, drive type, and how the unit is supported. The comparison below covers the first.</p>
<h2 id="comparison-heading">Spiral vs. VRC vs. Incline</h2>
